    "summary": "A young woman escapes a dangerous encounter with Wednesday by tricking her out of the house and sealing the door with crosses and prayer. The passage then discusses Friday, Wednesday, and Sunday as sainted or supernatural weekday figures connected with spinning taboos, quest assistance, animal lordship, and in one Slovak example the dismemberment and restoration of a youth. It closes by classifying such beings with other Slavic spirits and by introducing the Leshy tale as a reduced peasant form of a theft-and-recovery plot.",
